                  <msItem>
                     <title>Alhasen, Optica</title>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">Westminster Abbey 36 (nos. 4, 5), Bodleian 4o
                        C.95, and the fragments at Oxford, CCC, are all leaves from the same MS.
                        used in binding: cf. Ker, Pastedowns, p. xi. Four more leaves are at Merton
                        Coll.</note>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">MS. 490 no. 8 is the 1st leaf, it ends 'set
                        fuerint'. The opening words of the 2nd leaf were therefore 'ex colore
                        illius' (cf. Corpus MS. 150 fol. 1v; Sloane 306, fol. 1v).</note>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">Powicke, Books of Merton, no. 96 (2o folio: 'ex
                        colore illius').</note>
                  </msItem>
